# Coding Standards

# Coding Standards

* Follow the existing language and framework conventions.
* Prefer simple, readable, maintainable code.
* Avoid unnecessary abstraction.
* Keep functions and modules focused.
* Reuse existing utilities and services when appropriate.
* Do not duplicate business logic.
* Use meaningful names.
* Handle errors explicitly.
* Avoid silent failures.
* Do not leave debugging code, temporary logs, or commented-out dead code.
* Keep secrets and credentials out of source code.
* Use environment variables or the project's existing secret-management approach.
* Preserve backward compatibility unless a breaking change is required.

